ADDITIONAL NOTICE REGARDING APPLE PLATFORM ENTITLEMENTS

This project is a client-side implementation of standard, publicly documented
proxy protocols (SOCKS5 -- RFC 1928 / RFC 1929, and HTTP CONNECT -- RFC 9110)
plus an iOS Network Extension packet tunnel.

Running a Packet Tunnel Provider on a physical iOS device requires the Apple
entitlement `com.apple.developer.networking.networkextension` with the value
`packet-tunnel-provider`. That entitlement is only issuable to Apple Developer
Program members; it cannot be provisioned with a free Apple ID.

This project does not, and must not, attempt to circumvent Apple's entitlement
or code-signing system. See docs/ENTITLEMENTS-AND-SIGNING.md for the full,
honest analysis of what does and does not work under each signing method.
